Third-party code and scope of the license
==========================================

The MIT license in LICENSE covers the files written for this repository:

  - psi-bench/      the benchmark harness, web UI, suites and results
  - pepsi/e2e/      the end-to-end PEPSI driver
  - README.md, NOTICE, LICENSE, .gitignore at the repository root

The three folders below are third-party projects. They are included with their original commit history (the commits keep
their original authors) so that the benchmark can be reproduced against the exact versions that were measured. Each keeps
its own license and copyright. They are the work of their authors; please cite their papers.

volepsi/      https://github.com/ladnir/volepsi
              Implements "VOLE-PSI: Fast OPRF and Circuit-PSI from Vector-OLE" (Rindal and Schoppmann, EUROCRYPT 2021,
              https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/266) and "Blazing Fast PSI from Improved OKVS and Subfield VOLE"
              (https://eprint.iacr.org/2022/320). Measured commit: 1ecfe79.
              License: MIT, Copyright 2022 Visa (see volepsi/LICENSE).

BZS-MPSI/     https://github.com/orzcy/BZS-MPSI
              "Efficient Scalable Multi-Party Private Set Intersection(-Variants) from Bicentric Zero-Sharing",
              Gao et al., ACM CCS 2024, https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3658644.3690245. Measured commit: 096d4ad.
              License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 orzcy (see BZS-MPSI/LICENSE).
              It contains a modified copy of volePSI, with its own license in BZS-MPSI/volepsi_LICENSE.

pepsi/        https://github.com/RasoulAM/pepsi
              Mahdavi et al., "PEPSI: Practically Efficient Private Set Intersection in the Unbalanced Setting",
              USENIX Security 2024, https://www.usenix.org/conference/usenixsecurity24/presentation/mahdavi
              Original commit 6eab9dd (R. Akhavan Mahdavi, 2024-08-19).
              The upstream repository does not contain a license file. The code is the property of its authors and is
              included here, with attribution, only to make the benchmark reproducible. Commit d9cf35e on top of the
              original adds a pinned SEAL version, Windows support and a README. If the authors object to this
              inclusion, it will be removed.

The papers themselves are not included.
